        "raw": "[quote=\"torian\"]\n\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><b>Silverleaf wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">I have to admit I&#39;ve thought about it.&nbsp;After all, I did design a MLP crochet pattern last year.The difficult bit would be deciding on the colours, and getting the cutie marks to look perfect.Legacy - I guess white, blue mane/tail.Tachyon - white, red mane/tail, those red rings on her legs.Bunker - I&#39;d add layers of plating to bulk him up, not sure how the mane/tail would work.AZ - similar, what to do about the mane/tail?Wraith - got to have some purple, don&#39;t know what other colours. Tricky.&nbsp;</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;I&#39;d have AZ with a black body with blue highlights and an electric blue mohawk mane and tail.Wraith, not sure about the body, but her hoofs would be purple and she&#39;d have white wraps going up her legs and a cape going over her mane (black).Bunker is hard, but could you do occasional lines of &#39;bumps&#39; (not sure how to describe it) to represent bolts? That way you could enschew a mane/tail altogether.&nbsp;Also a quick suggestion about pony types. Legacy should be a pegasus. Tachyon and AZ should be unicorns. And Bunker and Wraith should be earth ponies. \n[/quote]\n \n\n Thanks, that&#39;s very helpful! \n\n I think Wraith&#39;s cape would have to go around her neck because there just isn&#39;t a good way to fix a cape on a crocheted pony&#39;s head without the weight pulling the head down. \n\n I totally have ideas about Bunker&#39;s armour and you&#39;re right, bolts would be cool and I can definitely do that. Likely little black dots because crocheting&#39;s already pretty bumpy so they&#39;d need to be huge to stand out and that would look weird. A pony in a power suit is a fun idea! \n\n I hadn&#39;t thought at all about pony types, so that&#39;s a fantastic suggestion. :) \n\n Also, this might not actually happen, and if it does it will likely be a while before I find time to get started. \n",
